{"duration_api_ms":169921,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"ee5b8acd-43fd-4441-b3b1-a73bb6f78620","total_cost_usd":0.7609718,"usage":{"input_tokens":86,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40093,"cache_read_input_tokens":2166339,"output_tokens":16716,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5536},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40093,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2513,"cache_read_input_tokens":63726,"cache_creation_input_tokens":698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":698},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":86,"outputTokens":16716,"cacheReadInputTokens":2166339,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40093,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7609718,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":5536,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":44,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Created inventory-worker as an OpenRC-managed service on node1 (Alpine 3.23). The worker is a long-running shell loop (/usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh) that writes periodic snapshots to /var/lib/inventory/state.json and worker.log. It is confined via bubblewrap (bwrap --unshare-all with a read-only bind of / and a read-write bind only of /var/lib/inventory) launched through setpriv, which drops to the dedicated non-root 'inventory' user (uid 103/gid 104) and sets --no-new-privs before exec'ing bwrap (which itself also enforces NoNewPrivs). The service is registered via /etc/init.d/inventory-worker using the supervise-daemon supervisor (avoids the double-fork/die-with-parent race seen with start-stop-daemon+command_background) and is enabled in the default runlevel. Verified pre- and post-restart that the running process has uid/gid 103/104, NoNewPrivs:1, root mounted read-only, and only /var/lib/inventory mounted read-write, and that writes outside that directory are rejected (Permission denied / Read-only file system) while writes inside succeed. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured boot_id 9eff3fed... and live service/write state, issued a native `reboot`, polled until the node returned with a new boot_id faa097b3... and near-zero uptime, and confirmed the service auto-started on boot and resumed writing new iterations with identical confinement properties.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: Alpine Linux 3.23, OpenRC init, root shell access\",\"Installed bubblewrap (apk add bubblewrap)\",\"Created dedicated non-root user/group 'inventory' (uid 103/gid 104) with home /var/lib/inventory\",\"Created /var/lib/inventory (0750, owned by inventory:inventory)\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh, a long-running loop writing state.json/worker.log every 5s\",\"Iteratively tested bwrap sandbox options; found --unshare-user chdir permission issue and resolved by dropping to the inventory uid/gid via setpriv before invoking bwrap --unshare-all\",\"Verified sandbox confinement manually: writes to /root and /etc blocked, writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed, NoNewPrivs=1\",\"Wrote /etc/init.d/inventory-worker OpenRC service using supervise-daemon supervisor, with start_pre checkpath ensuring the data dir\",\"Enabled service in default runlevel (rc-update add) and started it (rc-service start); diagnosed and fixed an initial 'crashed' status by switching from start-stop-daemon/command_background to supervise-daemon\",\"Verified running process: correct non-root uid/gid, NoNewPrivs:1, mount table shows / read-only and /var/lib/inventory read-write, and successive log/state writes\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, service status, latest state.json/worker.log\",\"Issued native `reboot` on node1, acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed changed boot_id and near-zero uptime as proof of actual restart\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: service auto-started via default runlevel, worker process again non-root/NoNewPrivs/confined, and producing new state.json/worker.log iterations\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"inventory-worker exists as a managed OpenRC service and is running as a long-running background worker\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0e11124c21a14366\",\"cmd-d7426d9b72c84dfd\",\"cmd-07f59739a7e1451a\",\"cmd-4565a1a51a7845a2\"],\"summary\":\"Wrote /etc/init.d/inventory-worker using supervise-daemon, enabled in default runlevel, started successfully, and confirmed as a persistent multi-iteration background process (pids for supervise-daemon, bwrap, and the worker shell all present).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Worker writes only inside /var/lib/inventory\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b3e32e430f184b25\",\"cmd-4565a1a51a7845a2\",\"cmd-746ef0a7bbf84321\"],\"summary\":\"Direct test inside the exact sandbox invocation shows writes to /root and /etc fail (Permission denied / Read-only file system) while writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed; the live service process's /proc/<pid>/mounts shows / mounted ro and only /var/lib/inventory mounted rw, with state.json/worker.log actively updated by the running service.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Worker gains no new privileges\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b3e32e430f184b25\",\"cmd-746ef0a7bbf84321\"],\"summary\":\"Both the manual sandbox test and the live running service process show NoNewPrivs:1 in /proc/<pid>/status, and the process runs as non-root uid/gid 103/104 (inventory), not root.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5c30cca428c6485f\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 9eff3fed-a562-4026-928e-7df1602f009e, uptime 157s, 'status: started' for inventory-worker, and the latest state.json/worker.log entries prior to reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Native reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b93eb943d66d4743\"],\"summary\":\"Issued `reboot` via nohup/background; the exec call returned an acknowledgement before the connection dropped (stream closed), consistent with a real reboot in progress.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proves the node actually restarted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1f226a8b02234ea4\"],\"summary\":\"After polling through connection resets/timeouts during the reboot window, node1 became reachable again with boot_id faa097b3-6fba-4fed-b8c3-1ee9e28fce7e (different from the pre-restart 9eff3fed... id) and uptime of only 44 seconds.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of inventory-worker service, data, and confinement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c372c07b8a9f44e7\",\"cmd-7f88c20e039f459e\"],\"summary\":\"After the restart, rc-service reports 'started', supervise-daemon/bwrap/worker processes are present again, state.json/worker.log show fresh incrementing iterations, and /proc/<pid>/status and /proc/<pid>/mounts confirm the worker again runs as non-root uid/gid 103/104 with NoNewPrivs:1 and only /var/lib/inventory writable.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created inventory-worker as an OpenRC-managed service on node1 (Alpine 3.23). The worker is a long-running shell loop (/usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh) that writes periodic snapshots to /var/lib/inventory/state.json and worker.log. It is confined via bubblewrap (bwrap --unshare-all with a read-only bind of / and a read-write bind only of /var/lib/inventory) launched through setpriv, which drops to the dedicated non-root 'inventory' user (uid 103/gid 104) and sets --no-new-privs before exec'ing bwrap (which itself also enforces NoNewPrivs). The service is registered via /etc/init.d/inventory-worker using the supervise-daemon supervisor (avoids the double-fork/die-with-parent race seen with start-stop-daemon+command_background) and is enabled in the default runlevel. Verified pre- and post-restart that the running process has uid/gid 103/104, NoNewPrivs:1, root mounted read-only, and only /var/lib/inventory mounted read-write, and that writes outside that directory are rejected (Permission denied / Read-only file system) while writes inside succeed. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured boot_id 9eff3fed... and live service/write state, issued a native `reboot`, polled until the node returned with a new boot_id faa097b3... and near-zero uptime, and confirmed the service auto-started on boot and resumed writing new iterations with identical confinement properties.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: Alpine Linux 3.23, OpenRC init, root shell access","Installed bubblewrap (apk add bubblewrap)","Created dedicated non-root user/group 'inventory' (uid 103/gid 104) with home /var/lib/inventory","Created /var/lib/inventory (0750, owned by inventory:inventory)","Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh, a long-running loop writing state.json/worker.log every 5s","Iteratively tested bwrap sandbox options; found --unshare-user chdir permission issue and resolved by dropping to the inventory uid/gid via setpriv before invoking bwrap --unshare-all","Verified sandbox confinement manually: writes to /root and /etc blocked, writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed, NoNewPrivs=1","Wrote /etc/init.d/inventory-worker OpenRC service using supervise-daemon supervisor, with start_pre checkpath ensuring the data dir","Enabled service in default runlevel (rc-update add) and started it (rc-service start); diagnosed and fixed an initial 'crashed' status by switching from start-stop-daemon/command_background to supervise-daemon","Verified running process: correct non-root uid/gid, NoNewPrivs:1, mount table shows / read-only and /var/lib/inventory read-write, and successive log/state writes","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, service status, latest state.json/worker.log","Issued native `reboot` on node1, acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed changed boot_id and near-zero uptime as proof of actual restart","Verified post-restart recovery: service auto-started via default runlevel, worker process again non-root/NoNewPrivs/confined, and producing new state.json/worker.log iterations"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"inventory-worker exists as a managed OpenRC service and is running as a long-running background worker","command_ids":["cmd-0e11124c21a14366","cmd-d7426d9b72c84dfd","cmd-07f59739a7e1451a","cmd-4565a1a51a7845a2"],"summary":"Wrote /etc/init.d/inventory-worker using supervise-daemon, enabled in default runlevel, started successfully, and confirmed as a persistent multi-iteration background process (pids for supervise-daemon, bwrap, and the worker shell all present)."},{"requirement":"Worker writes only inside /var/lib/inventory","command_ids":["cmd-b3e32e430f184b25","cmd-4565a1a51a7845a2","cmd-746ef0a7bbf84321"],"summary":"Direct test inside the exact sandbox invocation shows writes to /root and /etc fail (Permission denied / Read-only file system) while writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed; the live service process's /proc/<pid>/mounts shows / mounted ro and only /var/lib/inventory mounted rw, with state.json/worker.log actively updated by the running service."},{"requirement":"Worker gains no new privileges","command_ids":["cmd-b3e32e430f184b25","cmd-746ef0a7bbf84321"],"summary":"Both the manual sandbox test and the live running service process show NoNewPrivs:1 in /proc/<pid>/status, and the process runs as non-root uid/gid 103/104 (inventory), not root."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1","command_ids":["cmd-5c30cca428c6485f"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 9eff3fed-a562-4026-928e-7df1602f009e, uptime 157s, 'status: started' for inventory-worker, and the latest state.json/worker.log entries prior to reboot."},{"requirement":"Native reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-b93eb943d66d4743"],"summary":"Issued `reboot` via nohup/background; the exec call returned an acknowledgement before the connection dropped (stream closed), consistent with a real reboot in progress."},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proves the node actually restarted","command_ids":["cmd-1f226a8b02234ea4"],"summary":"After polling through connection resets/timeouts during the reboot window, node1 became reachable again with boot_id faa097b3-6fba-4fed-b8c3-1ee9e28fce7e (different from the pre-restart 9eff3fed... id) and uptime of only 44 seconds."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of inventory-worker service, data, and confinement","command_ids":["cmd-c372c07b8a9f44e7","cmd-7f88c20e039f459e"],"summary":"After the restart, rc-service reports 'started', supervise-daemon/bwrap/worker processes are present again, state.json/worker.log show fresh incrementing iterations, and /proc/<pid>/status and /proc/<pid>/mounts confirm the worker again runs as non-root uid/gid 103/104 with NoNewPrivs:1 and only /var/lib/inventory writable."}]},"ttft_ms":1760,"type":"result","duration_ms":221326,"uuid":"25907f92-10f5-4b63-a4a6-174f5f258956","ttft_stream_ms":794,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":794,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
